ding is treated as `changes` (the job succeeds and the comment says so).\n-5. **Close-out.** The controller posts one PR review at the pinned commit (event `COMMENT`): findings on lines the PR added are inline comments, every other finding is listed in the review body. If GitHub answers 422 (a line or the commit is not in the PR), it posts the review again with every finding in the body, and if that is also refused, as a plain PR comment. It commits `review-<role>.md` and the run's redacted output to the PR branch through the per-branch committer (no `[skip ci]`: PR-branch commits always run CI so required checks report on the head), and swaps `:running` for `:done` or `:changes`. The reviewer never marks the PR ready and never edits it; the merger does.\n+5. **Close-out.** The controller posts one PR review at the pinned commit (event `COMMENT`): findings on lines the PR added are inline comments, every other finding is listed in the review body. If GitHub answers 422 (a line or the commit is not in the PR), it posts the review again with every finding in the body, and if that is also refused, as a plain PR comment. It commits `review-<role>.md` and the run's redacted output to the PR branch through the per-branch committer (no `[skip ci]`: PR-branch commits always run CI so required checks report on the head), and swaps `:running` for `:done` or `:changes`. The reviewer never edits the PR. After a close-out (and on every tick, so a restart cannot miss it) the controller marks a draft worker PR ready for review once every requested review is `:done` at the PR's current head and no `:changes`, `:running`, `ard:executor:failed`, `ard:needs-human`, `ard:hold` or `ard:tests:failed` label is present; it never converts a PR back to draft and never merges, which stays with the merger (Phase 2) and humans.\n 6. **A moved head is not a pass.** Just before close-out the loop compares the branch with the pinned commit. If it gained code outside `.ard/<issue#>/` meanwhile, a `changes` verdict is still posted and labelled (it is the conservative one), but an `approve` is posted without `:done`: the request label stays and the review runs again on the new head. The reviewed commit is recorded in the close-out record so the merger (#46) must re-verify that no code changed since `Plan.Review.CommitSHA` before merging: a small window remains between the head check and close-out adding `:done`. A review closed out by the Reaper after a restart has no head information, so an approve is treated as stale.\n \n **The starter reviewer (`reviewers/eng-review`, #36).** `.ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` checks correctness, missing tests and drift from `plan.md`. Its inputs, all untrusted, are `diff.patch`, `issue.md`, `comments.md` and the committed `.ard/<issue#>/`; text in the change that addresses a reviewer is a blocking `high` finding on its line (verdict `changes`), and the same text in the issue, comments or `.ard/<issue#>/` is ignored and mentioned in the body. It runs the repository's own linter and the changed packages' tests with coverage through Bash, writing scratch files outside the worktree, reports only problems on added lines and skips a check it cannot run, saying so; the package manager may fetch declared dependencies and nothing else is downloaded. Critical and high findings always block, medium only when it is a real bug, low and info never; a missing test blocks only when it is `high` (risky or core logic, or a case `plan.md` named), smaller gaps are `medium`. The verdict is `changes` exactly when a finding blocks. `line` is the head-side line: a `+` line goes inline, anything else in the body. It writes only `review-eng-review.md` with `role: eng-review`, `attempt: 1`, `status` `done` or `needs-human`, `findings` with a double-quoted `file` and a `message: |` block, never `next` or `worker`, and a body with a `## Checks` section. It answers `needs-human` only when there is nothing to review or the issue and the plan contradict each other. The starter override is Sonnet 5.5 with the default 30m timeout and no `when:`, so every PR from the starter worker gets it. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55.\ndiff --git a/docs/runbooks/gate-2.md b/docs/runbooks/gate-2.md\nindex 35d3b1a..e7b969c 100644\n--- a/docs/runbooks/gate-2.md\n+++ b/docs/runbooks/gate-2.md\n@@ -79,8 +79,9 @@ eng-review, and a human merges it. About an hour and a few dollars.\n    - `ard:review:eng-review` on the PR, then a PR review and\n      `ard:review:eng-review:done` or `:changes`\n 6. **Merge** the PR by hand once you are satisfied: the worker opens it as a\n-   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\n-   **Squash and merge**. Stop `serve` with Ctrl-C (SIGINT); it stops cleanly\n+   draft and the controller marks it ready once every requested review is\n+   `:done` at the head, so just **Squash and merge**. (Mark it ready by hand\n+   only to override a review that is still `:changes`.) Stop `serve` with Ctrl-C (SIGINT); it stops cleanly\n    between jobs.\n \n **Moving faster than the poll.** Each loop ticks once at startup, then every\ndiff --git a/internal/reviewer/doc.go b/internal/reviewer/doc.go\nindex 0d8855b..2e74fd2 100644\n--- a/internal/reviewer/doc.go\n+++ b/internal/reviewer/doc.go\n@@ -42,9 +42,20 @@\n // one COMMENT review at the pinned commit (inline comments on lines the PR\n // added, everything else in the body) and swaps the label: :done, :changes, or\n // (an approve on a head that gained code meanwhile) neither, so the request\n-// stays and the review runs again. The loop never marks the PR ready and never\n-// edits it; #46 does.\n+// stays and the review runs again. The loop never edits the PR.\n //\n-// In --dry-run the loop logs review.would_claim and stops: no fetch, no job\n+// # Marking ready\n+//\n+// After each close-out, and on every tick (so a restart cannot miss it), the\n+// loop marks a draft App PR on a worker/ branch ready for review when every\n+// requested review role is :done at the PR's current head (the head recorded\n+// by its newest claim, ignoring commits that only touch .ard/<issue>/), and\n+// none of :changes, :running, ard:executor:failed, ard:needs-human, ard:hold or\n+// ard:tests:failed is set. It logs review.marked_ready; a failed MarkReady is\n+// logged and retried next tick, never failing close-out. In --dry-run only the\n+// effects ledger gets a line. It never converts a PR back to draft and never\n+// merges.\n+//\n+// In --dry-run the loop logs review.would_claim and stops claiming: no fetch, no job\n // row, no pool slot, no label.\n package reviewer\ndiff --git a/internal/reviewer/loop.go b/internal/reviewer/loop.go\nindex b97fa54..6b1d1e4 100644\n--- a/internal/reviewer/loop.go\n+++ b/internal/reviewer/loop.go\n@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ type Effects interface {\n \tAddLabels(ctx context.Context, n int, labels ...string) error\n \tRemoveLabel(ctx context.Context, n int, label string) error\n \tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n+\tMarkReady(ctx context.Context, n int) error\n \tDryRun() bool\n }\n \n@@ -56,6 +57,7 @@ type Store interface {\n \tRunningJobs(ctx context.Context) ([]state.Job, error)\n \tAdmission(ctx context.Context, issue int) (state.Admission, error)\n \tSetAdmission(ctx context.Context, a state.Admission) error\n+\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n }\n \n // Finisher is *reaper.Finisher: the one way a started job ends.\n@@ -162,6 +164,14 @@ func (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, env controller.Env) error {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\n \tdry := l.d.Effects.DryRun()\n+\tid, err := l.d.Reader.Identity(ctx)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"review: identify github user: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tt := &tick{l: l, cfg: cfg, log: log, self: id.Login, dry: dry}\n+\t// The sweep needs no agent, so it runs before the credential check.\n+\tt.sweepReady(ctx)\n \tif _, err := l.d.Model.Require(); err != nil && !dry {\n \t\tl.mu.Lock()\n \t\tfirst := !l.noCred\n@@ -173,12 +183,6 @@ func (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, env controller.Env) error {\n \t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\n-\tid, err := l.d.Reader.Identity(ctx)\n-\tif err != nil {\n-\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n-\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"review: identify github user: %w\", err)\n-\t}\n-\tt := &tick{l: l, cfg: cfg, log: log, self: id.Login, dry: dry}\n \tcands, errs := t.candidates(ctx)\n \n \tif dry {\ndiff --git a/internal/reviewer/ready.go b/internal/reviewer/ready.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1d508ec\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/reviewer/ready.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@\n+package reviewer\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n+)\n+\n+// sweepReady re-checks the open draft worker PRs, so a PR whose last review\n+// finished before a restart still gets marked. Errors are logged, never\n+// returned: a failed sweep must not fail the tick.\n+func (t *tick) sweepReady(ctx context.Context) {\n+\tif len(t.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer)) == 0 {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n+\tfor _, role := range t.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer) {\n+\t\tq := `is:pr is:open label:\"` + labels.Done(labels.StageReview, role.Name) + `\"`\n+\t\thits, err := t.l.d.Reader.SearchIssues(ctx, q, github.SearchOpts{Sort: \"created\", Order: \"asc\", Max: 50})\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.log.Warn(\"review.ready_sweep_failed\", \"role\", role.Name, \"error\", err)\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tfor _, hit := range hits {\n+\t\t\tif seen[hit.Number] {\n+\t\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tseen[hit.Number] = true\n+\t\t\tt.maybeReady(ctx, hit.Number)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// maybeReady